al shift.", "watch": "Fresh district polling showing Giménez below 50 percent against Ehr, or new outside spending entering the race, would move it toward Lean R.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert rater lists this race; treated as safe for the party holding the seat.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Carlos A. Giménez (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Florida's 28th District, spanning the Florida Keys and western Miami-Dade, leans Republican by about ten points, and incumbent Carlos Giménez is seeking another term. He has raised roughly $600,000 and holds about $693,000 on hand, while Democrat Phil Ehr has kept pace with about $438,000 raised and $455,000 in the bank. Prediction markets give Giménez roughly a 94 percent chance of winning.\n\nEhr has run a visible campaign, collecting endorsements from national security figures, a former Defense Secretary, a labor union, and members of Congress, and he has pressed for debates while veterans tour the district on his behalf. Independent Eddy Rojas is also on the ballot but shows little fundraising activity. The only available poll is an early, hypothetical March survey showing Giménez at 46 percent, which offers limited guidance. With no expert ratings published, the race rests on the district's Republican lean, the incumbent's structural advantages, and market pricing, all pointing to a Giménez win.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1198, "margin": -8.92}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1112, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1123, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1336, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1022, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0826, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1109, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1143, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1436, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01",